```

# File.exist?

exist?(String path) -> bool

Whether the file is there

```ruby
return unless File.exist?(path)
```

# File#gets

gets() -> String?

Read one line

nil at the end of the file. The newline is still on the string.
```ruby
while (line = f.gets)
  handle(line.chomp)
end
```

# File.open

open(String path, String mode) -> File

Open a file

**Pass a block** and it closes on the way out. The mode is `"r"`, `"w"`
or `"a"`. There is no `File.binread`; use `read`.
```ruby
File.open("/home/a.txt", "r") do |f|
  body = f.read
end
```

# File#read

read() -> String

Read the whole thing

The whole file lands in memory at once. For a big one, loop on `gets`.
```ruby
body = f.read
```

# File#write

write(String str) -> Integer

Write to the file

It gives back how many bytes went out.
```ruby
f.write("hello\n")
```
