# SpriteImage#destroy

destroy() -> void

Let go of this image

```ruby
img.destroy
```

# SpriteImage#draw

draw() -> void

Draw into this image (inside the block)

```ruby
img.draw do |g|
  g.fill_rect(0, 0, 16, 16,
              FmrbGfx::RED)
end
```

# SpriteImage#height

height() -> Integer

Image height in pixels

```ruby
h = img.height
```

# SpriteImage#id

id() -> Integer

This image's number

What you hand to `FmrbGfx` directly.
```ruby
gfx.draw_image(img.id, x: 10, y: 20)
```

# SpriteImage#load_bmp

load_bmp(String path) -> void

Read a BMP file into this image

**BMP only**; PNG goes through `FmrbGfx#create_image`. It is decoded on
the graphics side.
```ruby
img.load_bmp(
  "/usr/share/sprites/flappy/bird_up.bmp")
```

# SpriteImage.new

new(FmrbGfx gfx) -> SpriteImage

Make an image (the size is in pixels)

**Takes keyword arguments**; the signature is positional because the type
engine has none.
```ruby
img = SpriteImage.new(gfx,
      width: 16, height: 16,
      transparent_color: 0x00,
      use_transparent: true)
```

# SpriteImage#reset_target

reset_target() -> void

Draw on the screen again

```ruby
img.reset_target
```

# SpriteImage#set_target

set_target() -> void

Draw into this image from now on

**Remember to send it back.** `draw` does both ends for you.

