# TileMap#event_at

event_at(Integer x, Integer y) -> Hash?

The event on that square

```ruby
ev = map.event_at(@x, @y)
handle(ev) if ev
```

# TileMap#events

events() -> Array

The events placed on the map

```ruby
map.events.length
```

# TileMap#height

height() -> Integer

The map's height in tiles

```ruby
h = map.height
```

# TileMap#layers

layers() -> Array

The layers of the map

```ruby
map.layers.length
```

# TileMap.new

new(String json_path) -> TileMap

Load a map file

**Give it the `.map.bin`.** JSON works and is far slower on a device --
39 seconds against 55 milliseconds.
```ruby
map = TileMap.new("/app/img/world.map.bin")
```

# TileMap#render

render(TileSheet sheet) -> void

Draw the whole map

Draws the whole map. For a large one use `render_view`, which draws only
what is on screen.

# TileMap#render_view

render_view(TileSheet sheet) -> void

Draw only what is in sight

**Takes keyword arguments.**
```ruby
map.render_view(sheet,
  view_x: @cam_x, view_y: @cam_y,
  view_w: 320, view_h: 240)
```

# TileMap#spawn_x

spawn_x() -> Integer

Where the player starts

```ruby
@x = map.spawn_x
```

# TileMap#spawn_y

spawn_y() -> Integer

Where the player starts

```ruby
@y = map.spawn_y
```

# TileMap#tile_at

tile_at(Integer x, Integer y) -> Integer?

The tile number at that square

nil outside the map. The coordinates are **tiles**, not pixels.
```ruby
t = map.tile_at(3, 5)
```

# TileMap#tile_size

tile_size() -> Integer

One tile's size in pixels

```ruby
px = map.tile_size
```

